      "answer": "s and their payloads.\n\n### **Option 2: Add Temporary Logging to a Specific Provider**\nEdit the provider's stream function (e.g., `apps/server/providers/src/devin/stream-fn.ts`) and add logging before the fetch call:\n\n```typescript\n// Around line 138 in stream-fn.ts\nconsole.log('📤 Devin Request Body:', {\n  bodySize: frame.length,\n  bodyHex: Array.from(frame).slice(0, 100).map(b =\u003e b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join(' '),\n  headers: {\n    'content-type': 'application/connect+proto',\n    'connect-protocol-version': '1',\n    // ... other headers\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### **Option 3: Add a Global Fetch Wrapper (Production-ready)**\nCreate `apps/server/providers/src/fetch-interceptor.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nconst originalFetch = global.fetch;\nglobal.fetch = async (input, init) =\u003e {\n  console.log('📤 HTTP Request:', {\n    url: input,\n    method: init?.method || 'GET',\n    headers: init?.headers,\n    bodyLength: init?.body ? new Blob([init.body]).size : 0,\n  });\n  const response = await originalFetch(input, init);\n  console.log('📥 HTTP Response:', response.status, response.statusText);\n  return response;\n};\n```\n\nThen import it at the top of `apps/server/index.ts`:\n```typescript\nimport './providers/src/fetch-interceptor.js';\n```\n\n### **Option 4: Use System-Level Tools**\nFor HTTPS traffic inspection (outside the app):\n```bash\n# macOS with mitmproxy\nmitmproxy --mode reverse:http://localhost:3000 -p 8080\n# Then point your client to proxy through port 8080\n```\n\n### **Option 5: Check the Daemon Logs**\nIf running in daemon mode, logs go to:\n```bash\n~/.console/logs/daemon.log  # or ~/.console-dev/logs/daemon.log in dev mode\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Which Should You Use?**\n- **Quick one-time debug**: Option 1 (Bun inspect)\n- **Temporary logging**: Option 2 (add to specific provider)\n- **Permanent debugging setup**: Option 3 (global interceptor) or Option 4 (mitmproxy for HTTPS)\n\nWould you like me to add a global fetch interceptor to the codebase, or would you prefer to debug a specific provider?"
